int (Freestyle), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350066"} "15 kilometres (Classical), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350068"} "30 kilometres Skiathlon, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350069"} "4 × 10 kilometres Relay, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350070"} "Team Sprint (Classical), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350075"} "Sprint (Freestyle), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350087"} "10 kilometres (Classical), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350088"} "30 kilometres (Mass Start, Freestyle), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350089"} "15 kilometres Skiathlon, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350090"} "4 × 5 kilometres Relay, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350091"} "Team Sprint (Classical), Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "1890"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "1892"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "1894"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "1896"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "1902"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "1908"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "1916"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "1927"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "1938"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "1950"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "1962"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "1974"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "1987"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "2000"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "2014"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "2031"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "2051"} "1994"] "\n" [:option {:value "2071"} "1998"] "\n" [:option {:value "2091"} "2002"] "\n" [:option {:value "2134"} "2006"] "\n" [:option {:value "923554"} "2010"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000278"} "2018"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019713"} "2022"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000134"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/187"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "50 kilometres (Mass Start, Freestyle), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "23 February 2014 — 11:00"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/889"} "Kompleks Dlya Sorevnovaniy Po Lyzhnym Gonkam i Biatlonu Laura, Mountain Cluster, Krasnaya Polyana"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/350067"} "64 from 26 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Course Length: 49,735 m" [:br {}] "Height Differential: 90 m" [:br {}] "Intermediate 1: 12.5 km" [:br {}] "Intermediate 2: 25.0 km" [:br {}] "Intermediate 3: 38.0 km" [:br {}] "Maximum Climb: 56 m" [:br {}] "Total Climbing: 1,790 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "In the last and longest cross-country race, the 50 km freestyle mass start, the leading group comprised over half the field at the mid-point. Just after the 30 km point Finland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/118810"} "Matti Heikkinen"] " broke away gaining a lead of over 20 seconds. However, a chasing pack of four closed the gap and brought with them most of the field, catching Heikkinen within five kilometers. As the field of about 60 skiers started the final 5 km lap, the Swede " [:a {:href "/athletes/109816"} "Anders Södergren"] " was in the lead. With just two kilometers to go his compatriot " [:a {:href "/athletes/118751"} "Daniel Richardsson"] " was in front, but no one managed to gain a decisive lead. Double gold medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/118753"} "Dario Cologna"] " from Switzerland, who could be seen close to the vanguard throughout the race, was the unlucky fellow on the day, breaking his ski while in fourth place with less than two kilometers to go. The race was effectively decided on the last climb, where the Russians showed their strength. A four-man group of three Russians, " [:a {:href "/athletes/109828"} "Aleksandr Legkov"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/118800"} "Maksim Vylegzhanin"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/128326"} "Ilya Chernousov"] ", and Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/118807"} "Martin Johnsrud Sundby"] " entered the stadium clear of the field. With the end almost in sight Legkov overtook Vylegzhanin to move into the pole position and held it to the finish. In a close sprint to the line Vylegzhanin just held on for the silver medal ahead of compatriot Chernousov in a photo finish. Sundby missed out on a medal, finishing just one second behind the winner."] "\n\n" [:p {} "It was the first time in 78 years that athletes from one country achieved a clean sweep in this event; the last time was by Sweden at Garmisch-Partenkirchen. Legkov had turned down the opportunity to carry the Russian flag at the Opening Ceremony because he thought it would be bad for him to leave altitude."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In May 2016 WADA (World Anti-Doping Agency) commissioned a report, the McLaren Report, to look into allegations of systematic Russian doping and a cover-up to avoid positives at the 2014 Sochi Winter Olympics. The report was released in two parts, in July and December 2016, and confirmed the allegations. In 2017 the IOC formed a commission to investigate this, headed by IOC Member " [:a {:href "/athletes/39778"} "Denis Oswald"] ", and usually referred to as the Oswald Commission. In late October 2017 the Oswald Commission began to release its findings."] "\n\n" [:p {} "One of the first findings was to implicate Aleksandr Legkov, the gold medalist in this event. Legkov was disqualified and his medal effectively removed. He immediately appealed to the Court of Arbitration for Sport (CAS). Eight days later, the silver medalist, Maksim Vylegzhanin, was also disqualified. About 10 days before the " [:a {:href "/games/60/overview"} "PyeongChang Winter Olympics"] " began, the CAS reached a decision and Legkov and Vylegzhanin were exonerated and their medals were restored."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the case of Legkov, the IOC actually appealed the decision of the CAS to the Swiss Federal Tribunal, which upheld the decision of the CAS, which meant that Legkov was exonerated and his gold medal status restored."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button613148", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button613148').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Intermediate 1"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Intermediate 2"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Intermediate 3"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/109828"} "Aleksandr Legkov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RUS.png"}] "RUS"]] [:td {} "1-46:55.2"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "26:53.4 (=2)"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "53:18.2 (9)"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "1-20:13.4 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:class "footnote", :href "#", :title "Disqualified after findings from Oswald Commission Report, but later exonerated by the CAS.", :data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right"} "1"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "7"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/118800"} "Maksim Vylegzhanin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RUS.png"}] "RUS"]] [:td {} "1-46:55.9"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "26:57.7 (16)"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "53:19.9 (14)"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: no